  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Implement Speculative Decoding and Token Verification** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef inference_speculative_decoding_verification(draft_tokens: list, draft_probs: list, target_probs: list) -> dict:\n    acc = []\n    for i, tok in enumerate(draft_tokens):\n        ratio = min(1.0, float(target_probs[i]) / max(float(draft_probs[i]), 1e-12))\n        if ratio >= 0.8: acc.append(tok)\n        else: break\n    return {'accepted_tokens': acc, 'num_accepted': len(acc), 'acceptance_rate': round(len(acc)/max(len(draft_tokens), 1), 4)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
